PROTOCOL KCL/1
SYNTAX response_header="KCL/1"
SYNTAX result="OK|READY|WARN|ERROR <operation>"
SEMANTIC FACT="verified observation"
SEMANTIC READY="accepted but bounded further authorization is required"
AUTH session_open="?q=AUTH_SESSION_OPEN&code=<6digits>; legacy/fallback transport, not internal policy gate"
AUTH status="?q=AUTH_STATUS"
AUTH critical_prepare="?q=AUTH_APPROVAL_PREPARE&action=self_update_install&session_id=<id>&token=<rolling>"
AUTH critical_execute="?q=AUTH_APPROVAL_EXECUTE&approval_id=<id>&code=<6digits>"
AUTONOMY source_list="?q=AUTONOMY_SOURCE_LIST&session_id=<id>&token=<rolling>"
AUTONOMY source_read="?q=AUTONOMY_SOURCE_READ&path=<manifest-path>&offset=<n>&session_id=<id>&token=<rolling>"
AUTONOMY upload="AUTONOMY_UPLOAD_BEGIN -> CHUNK -> FINISH"
AUTONOMY deploy="?q=AUTONOMY_DEPLOY&target=<alias>&..."
ARCHIVE status="?q=ARCHIVE_STATUS"
RULE "Every authenticated autonomy request consumes its token and returns the next token"
RULE "Where FreeOTP remains required for a protected external action, it is current-step, one-use, 30 seconds and 6 digits."
RULE "Critical approvals bind action, target/version and SHA-256 before TOTP execution"
RULE "Legacy proposal/admin interfaces remain available as recovery paths"
AUTONOMY read_lease="source-only; 600s; 64 uses; no main-token rotation"
AUTONOMY compact_batch="base64url JSON over GET; up to 16 exact patch operations; one session rotation"
AUTONOMY release_prepare="server-side version/genome lineage metadata; candidate remains non-executable until normal verifier"
AUTONOMY transaction_buffer="BEGIN nonrotating -> APPEND <=1024-byte inert fragments -> COMMIT sha256 + one main-token rotation; max 64KiB/600s"
AUTH bound_red_ttl="3600s; execution still requires fresh one-use FreeOTP and exact binding recheck"
AUTONOMY adaptive_transaction_buffer="BEGIN(profile) returns safe/probe -> APPEND learns successful size -> BACKOFF records smaller transport ceiling -> COMMIT rotates once; duplicate last fragment is idempotent"
AUTH session_open_grace="default past_steps=2; current plus previous two TOTP counters accepted once for normal autonomy session opening only"
RULE "Technical RED classification alone does not imply human authorization; protected production/external authority remains human-gated."
CHAT_UPDATE status="?q=CHAT_UPDATE_STATUS"
CHAT_UPDATE chunked="CHAT_UPDATE_BEGIN(filename) -> CHAT_UPDATE_CHUNK(upload_id,seq,data) -> CHAT_UPDATE_FINISH(upload_id)"
CHAT_UPDATE raw_post="POST api.php?q=CHAT_UPDATE_RAW with X-KiCom-Session-Id, X-KiCom-Session-Token and optional X-KiCom-Filename"
CHAT_UPDATE authored="AUTONOMY_BUILD_BEGIN -> exact protected build patches -> AUTONOMY_BUILD_PREPARE_RELEASE -> AUTONOMY_BUILD_FINALIZE"
RULE "Direct chat update transport does not depend on Slack, mail, GitHub or another relay."
RULE "Chunked and raw direct package transfer converge on the ordinary self-update verifier."
RULE "Server-side authored builds are preferred when ChatGPT creates the update because no package re-transfer is necessary."
RULE "Transport acceptance is not installation authority; the update verifier and existing action boundary decide what happens next."
DEV auth="POST api.php?q=DEV_AUTH; WebAuthn passkey"
DEV api="POST api.php?q=DEV_API; X-KiCom-Dev-Session + X-KiCom-Dev-Token"
DEV bridge="GET /dev/agent/ or ?q=DEV_BRIDGE; same fixed DEV capability router"
RULE "DEV credentials are DEV-only and cannot cross into production, recovery, auth-admin, secrets or self-update-install authority."
RULE "Slack, Mail, GitHub and Opera/browser are transports/control surfaces and never authority sources."
SQLITE status="?q=SQLITE_STATUS"
SQLITE health="?q=SQLITE_HEALTH&session_id=...&token=..."
SQLITE snapshot="?q=SQLITE_SNAPSHOT&reason=...&session_id=...&token=..."
SQLITE heal="?q=SQLITE_HEAL&session_id=...&token=..."
SQLITE maintenance="?q=SQLITE_MAINTENANCE&session_id=...&token=..."
SQLITE evolution_status="?q=SQLITE_EVOLUTION_STATUS&session_id=...&token=..."
SQLITE evolution_tick="?q=SQLITE_EVOLUTION_TICK&session_id=...&token=..."
SQLITE diagnostics="?q=SQLITE_DIAGNOSTICS"
RULE "Stored migration checksums must match compiled migration definitions before the DB opens successfully."
RULE "Evolution promotion requires a successfully verified pre-snapshot."
RULE "SQLite writes are primary; compatibility mirrors remain reconstructable."
RULE "Corrupt DB files are quarantined, not hard-deleted."
RULE "DB evolution tests in shadow before live promotion."
END_PROTOCOL KCL/1
